    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42809" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scă_brĭtĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scă_brĭtĭes</span></b> , em,
			ē (in both forms post-Aug.; esp. freq. in Plin.),
			f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>roughness</i>, <i>ruggedness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">digitorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					34, 13, 34, § 131</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unguium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 9, 37, § 139</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linguae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 9, 45, § 100</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chartae levigatur dente,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					13, 12, 25, § 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corticis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					21, 4, 10, § 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferramentorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 9, 41, § 148</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arteriae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					27, 12, 105, § 130</span></i>
			 et saep.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The scab</i>, <i>the itch</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 5,
			8</span></i>.</div>
